WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 004, en. Timings estimated from the script.

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.154
<v a monk of Llandough>Earth to earth. Lie here with the others, your face to the east, toward the dawn.

2
00:00:14.504 --> 00:00:21.427
<v a woman of the district at the graveside>There are so many of them, brother. Row after row. Every winter, more. Will she be lonely here?

3
00:00:21.777 --> 00:00:33.315
<v a monk of Llandough>Lonely? Never. The brothers sing the psalms here every dusk, above the Ely. This little church was old when I came, and it will be here after we are gone.

4
00:00:33.665 --> 00:00:38.281
<v a woman of the district at the graveside>And under the turf, the old stones. The spades still strike them.

5
00:00:38.631 --> 00:00:47.092
<v a monk of Llandough>They are the Romans' stones. They are long gone; we are the ones who stay. Come. The brothers are waiting for us.
